1. The Examination Committee consists of:
a) Chairman: President or Vice President for Academic and Student Affairs;
b) Vice-Chairman: Vice President or Head of the Department of Academic and
Student Affairs;
c) Standing member: Head or Deputy Head of the Department of Academie and
Student Affairs;
d) Other members: some department heads, deans, academic coordinators of
relevant study programs and IT staff.
2. Responsibilities and rights of the Examination Committee:
a) To implement the admission modes which have been approved;
b) To respond to questions, complaints or protests related to student recruitment;
c) To collect and use examination and application fees;
d) To decide the admission scores based on the recommendations of the Admission
Board;
e) To make conclusion about the admission and to make decision on the matters are
not regulated in this regulation;
ñ To use appropriate entrance examination management software, to promptly
report the results of the entrance examination and student recruitment to the MoET
and other relevant managing bodies when needed.
g) To adjust the admission plan or postpone/cancel an admission mode in case of a
force majeure.
3. Responsibilities and rights of the Chairman:
a) To implement and be responsible for the undergraduate’s student recruitment;
b) To promptly report the results of the entrance examination and student
recruitment to the MoET and other relevant managing bodies;
c) To establish assistance boards for the Examination Committce in order to carry
out the student recruitment.
4. Vice-Chairman: to implement the responsibilities assigned by the Chairman and
carry out the tasks on behalf of the Chairman when delegated by the Chairman.
